%S A402525 1,1,2,5,17,82,547,5900,116975,4728427
%N A402525 Number of simple connected graphs on n unlabeled vertices whose eccentric vertices are all peripheral.
%C A402525 A vertex is an eccentric vertex if it is a vertex that is most distant from another vertex. It is peripheral if there is such a vertex where the distance is equal to the graph diameter. Every peripheral vertex is eccentric by definition.
%H A402525 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/GraphEccentricity.html">Graph Eccentricity</a>.
